      "Before the click, the selected endpoint is pw-output-1, data-output-action is activate and the label is Activate MIDI output.",
      "Across the same click, the operational renderer changes the label to Activate selected output and data-operational-action from output-toggle to activate.",
      "The MIDI status remains selected; no starting/live/error state is observed.",
      "The native click point is x1531.2/y37.59; the pre-click button box is x1467.796875/y23.59375/w126.8125/h28."
    ],
    "limit": "The trace establishes competing label writers and a failed activation. It does not conclusively identify the native event target at every pointer phase."
  },
  "implementation": [
    "The legacy controller computes the current base action/aria state, then delegates label presentation before writing any fallback label.",
    "The operational presenter reads the current readonly snapshot synchronously and uses the same label on its later scheduled redraw; Stop, Cancel discovery and Takeover remain base actions.",
    "A WeakMap records the current borrower and the first DOM/attribute origin. Superseded renderers and disposers cannot change or move successor-owned controls; reverse restoration preserves sibling order.",
    "Claim/release refreshes the current base presentation, stale-owner release is ignored, and the workstation refuses presentation after disposal."
